```cs
public virtual int Capacity
{
    get
    {
        return _items.Length;
    }
    set
    {
        if (value < _size)
        {
            throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException(Environment.GetResourceString("ArgumentOutOfRange_SmallCapacity"));
        }
        if (value != _items.Length)
        {
            if (value > 0)
            {
                Object[] newItems = new Object[value];
                if (_size > 0)
                {
                    Array.Copy(_items, 0, newItems, 0, _size);
                }
                _items = newItems;
            }
            else
            {
                _items = EmptyArray<Object>.Value;
            }
            _version++;
        }
    }
}
```

The commented line "@@@ size of array does not change after the operation" means that after the operation, the size of the array should remain the same. So, the assert statement should be:

```cs
Debug.Assert(OLD(Capacity) == _items.Length);
```

